== R-EXACT: FAIL
Decision on formatExact = FormatFloat(v,'g',15,64) for all values: it does NOT meet R-EXACT.
- R-EXACT requires stored values rendered 'f',-1 and "never re-rounded", and requires derived values "with no exponent".
- (a) 16-17 significant-digit stored values are re-rounded, and an untouched save rewrites them. The app can hold them:
  - S/js/typed.js: a user types 83.03712345678912 into Tax-Deferred % (step="any" accepts it).
  - POST "tax_deferred_percent=83.03712345678912" saves exactly "83.03712345678912".
  - After reload the input shows "83.0371234567891". An untouched settings save rewrites the stored value to "83.0371234567891".
  - Fixture S/fx/mk_exact.py, untouched saves, bit-exact changes:
    - taxable_cost_basis 12923.603942198184 -> 12923.6039421982
    - tax_deferred_percent 83.03712345678912 -> 83.0371234567891
    - portfolio_value 2437512.3400000003 -> 2437512.34
    - monthly_property_tax 666.6666666666666 -> 666.666666666667
    - fra_benefit 4114.912345678901 -> 4114.9123456789
    - roth annual_amount 12345.678901234567 -> 12345.6789012346
    - healthcare current_monthly_cost 612.3456789012345 -> 612.345678901234
  - The live plan already holds 17-significant-digit computed floats (removed_income_sources amount 10339.581296296297), and sync.go:249 divides. The lead's v4 oracle fails on the same class.
- (b) Exponent output in type=number inputs.
  - Served attribute values: property_tax_inflation 0.00005 -> value="5e-05"; floor_cut_pct -> "5e-05"; care_monthly_cost 0.00001 -> "1e-05".
  - The derived COLA ×100 path, cola_rate 1e-7 -> value="1e-05", is explicitly forbidden ("no exponent").
  - Chromium keeps "5e-05" as the visible field text.
- The worker's TestFormatExact claims "raw stored value renders with NO re-rounding" but has no case over 11 significant digits and no case below 0.001. So neither (a) nor (b) is pinned.
- Missing: 'f',-1 for stored values; a 15-significant-digit render without exponent for derived values; tests pinning both, e.g. 12923.603942198184 and 5e-05.
- Spec-level observation, not a worker defect: COLA ×100/÷100 cannot round-trip bit-exactly under either rule, because the handler divides by 100.
  - Sweep 0-0.1 step 1e-4: 266/1001 values mismatch with g15, 139/1001 with shortest.
  - Example 0.0145 -> 0.014499999999999999.
  - v4's COLA failure therefore needs a lead ruling (handler change vs tolerance).

